Third-party work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

keyboard_bequiet_lightmount_rgb
  https://github.com/bbossa/keyboard_bequiet_lightmount_rgb
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later (used here under GPL-3.0-or-later)

  The protocol layer and the device access of quietlinux-core are a Rust port of
  this project:
    crates/quietlinux-core/src/protocol.rs        <- lightmount/protocol.py
    crates/quietlinux-core/src/device.rs          <- lightmount/device.py
    crates/quietlinux-core/src/hid_descriptor.rs  <- lightmount/hid.py
    crates/quietlinux-core/src/layout.rs          <- lightmount/layout.py
    crates/quietlinux-core/src/keymap.rs          <- lightmount/keymap.py (LED indexes, positions, French legends)
    crates/quietlinux-cli/src/calibrate.rs        <- calibrate command of lightmount/cli.py
    crates/quietlinux-core/tests/protocol.rs      <- tests/test_protocol.py
  The test fixtures in crates/quietlinux-core/tests/fixtures/ are copied
  unchanged from its tests/fixtures/ directory.

Slint
  https://slint.dev
  License: GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-Slint-Royalty-free-2.0 OR
  LicenseRef-Slint-Software-3.0; used under GPL-3.0-only.
  quietlinux-gui is built with it, so that binary as a whole is distributed
  under GPL-3.0.

monsgeek-akko-linux
  https://github.com/echtzeit-solutions/monsgeek-akko-linux
  License: GPL-3.0
  No code is used. Its structure (separate protocol, transport and front ends)
  and its capture-based method inspired this project.

IO Center Web (be quiet!)
  https://iocenter.bequiet.com/
  Protocol facts (command numbers and names, enumerations, message layouts)
  were read from the JavaScript the web app serves to every browser, to make
  QuietLinux interoperable with the keyboard. No code from it is included;
  docs/protocol.md marks every such fact with [web].

